        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs one command line and returns its result without writing to a process stream. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The first argument is the verb. An empty list prints the banner and the help. The global options <computeroutput>--help</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>--version</computeroutput> are handled before a verb is matched.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>arguments</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The argument list, with the verb at index 0. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The text of the input, or nullopt when the process standard input is read.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The exit code, the output documents, and the failures. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
